   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Echo Stack\n\nA word focuses in at the center while outline copies of it unfold above and below and keep drifting, like the one clear line on a spinning drum.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A one-word statement (a value, a promise) should hold the screen for a while and still feel alive.\n- Repetition should add weight to a word without adding any other text.\n- A beat in a sequence of single words, where each word gets the same treatment and only the text changes.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The word should just appear and stay still: use focus-blur-resolve.\n- The repeats should run sideways as a strip of text: use infinite-marquee.\n- The screen should fill with rows of text rather than a column around one word: use type-wall.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Bold.\"\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- echo_color (color): Echo color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"up\"\n- font_size (number, 60-300): Font size, default 170\n- echoes (number, 1-6): Echoes per side, default 3\n- echo_opacity (number, 0.05-1): Echo opacity, default 0.35\n- cycle (number, 15-240): Frames per row, default 60\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Echo Stack\n\n  A word focuses in at the center while outline copies of it unfold above and below and keep drifting, like the one clear line on a spinning drum.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/echo-stack/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"echo-stack\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"One short word or phrase.\", \"default\": \"Bold.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Text color\", \"description\": \"Color of the centre word.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"echo_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Echo color\", \"description\": \"Color of the outline copies.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"direction\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Direction\", \"description\": \"Which way the echoes drift.\", \"default\": \"up\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"up\", \"label\": \"Up\"}, {\"value\": \"down\", \"label\": \"Down\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Text size in reference pixels (1280×720 stage).\", \"default\": 170, \"min\": 60, \"max\": 300, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"echoes\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Echoes per side\", \"description\": \"Outline copies above and below the word.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 6, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"echo_opacity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Echo opacity\", \"description\": \"Opacity of the strongest echo.\", \"default\": 0.35, \"min\": 0.05, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"cycle\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Frames per row\", \"description\": \"Frames the drift takes to move one row (30 fps).\", \"default\": 60, \"min\": 15, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Echo Stack</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@100..900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .es-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; }\n        .es-wrap { position: relative; }\n        .es-line { line-height: 1; white-space: pre; font-weight: 800; font-variation-settings: \"wght\" 800; }\n        .es-echo { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"echo-stack\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"es-clip\" class=\"es-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg width=\"0\" height=\"0\" style=\"position:absolute\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n            <defs>\n              <filter id=\"es-outline\">\n                <feMorphology id=\"es-erode\" in=\"SourceAlpha\" operator=\"erode\" radius=\"1.5\" result=\"inner\" />\n                <feComposite in=\"SourceAlpha\" in2=\"inner\" operator=\"out\" result=\"ring\" />\n                <feFlood id=\"es-flood\" flood-color=\"#fafafa\" />\n                <feComposite in2=\"ring\" operator=\"in\" />\n              </filter>\n            </defs>\n          </svg>\n          <div id=\"es-wrap\" class=\"es-wrap\">\n            <div id=\"es-main\" class=\"es-line\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Bold.\");\n            var color = col(vars.color, \"#fafafa\"), echoColor = col(vars.echo_color, color);\n            var echoes = Math.round(num(vars.echoes, 3, 1, 6)), echoOpacity = num(vars.echo_opacity, 0.35, 0.05, 1);\n            var cycle = num(vars.cycle, 60, 15, 240), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var sign = pick(vars.direction, [\"up\", \"down\"], \"up\") === \"down\" ? 1 : -1;\n            var unit = Math.min(root.clientWidth / 1280, root.clientHeight / 720);\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 170, 60, 300) * unit;\n            var wrap = document.getElementById(\"es-wrap\"), main = document.getElementById(\"es-main\");\n            // Keep the word inside the frame: shrink when it is wider than 90 % of the width.\n            main.textContent = text; main.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; main.style.color = color;\n            if (main.scrollWidth > root.clientWidth * 0.9) size = size * (root.clientWidth * 0.9) / main.scrollWidth;\n            main.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            document.getElementById(\"es-erode\").setAttribute(\"radius\", 1.5 * unit);\n            document.getElementById(\"es-flood\").setAttribute(\"flood-color\", echoColor);\n            var pitch = 1.05 * size, reach = echoes + 2, pool = [];\n            for (var k = -reach; k <= reach; k++) {\n              var d = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              d.className = \"es-line es-echo\"; d.textContent = text; d.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              d.style.color = echoColor; d.style.filter = \"url(#es-outline)\"; d.style.opacity = 0;\n              wrap.insertBefore(d, main); pool.push({ k: k, el: d });\n            }\n            var easeOutCubic = function (p) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3); };\n            function smooth(x) { var c = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, x)); return c * c * (3 - 2 * c); }\n            function fade(distance) {\n              var dd = Math.abs(distance);\n              if (dd < 0.55) return 0;\n              if (dd < 1) return smooth((dd - 0.55) / 0.45);\n              var r = Math.max(1, echoes + 0.5);\n              return Math.max(0, 1 - (dd - 1) / (r - 1));\n            }\n            tick(function (tt) {\n              var t = tt * 30 * speed;\n              var k1 = ip(t, 0, 14, 0, 1, easeOutCubic);\n              main.style.opacity = k1;\n              main.style.filter = 12 * (1 - k1) > 0.05 ? \"blur(\" + 12 * (1 - k1) * unit + \"px)\" : \"none\";\n              main.style.transform = \"scale(\" + (1.04 - 0.04 * k1) + \")\";\n              var phase = sign * ((t / cycle) % 1);\n              var spread = ip(t, 8, 26, 0.6, 1, easeOutCubic), fadeIn = ip(t, 8, 24, 0, 1, easeOutCubic);\n              pool.forEach(function (p) {\n                var offset = p.k + phase;\n                var op = echoOpacity * fadeIn * fade(offset);\n                p.el.style.opacity = op > 0 ? op : 0;\n                p.el.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, calc(-50% + \" + offset * spread * pitch + \"px))\";\n              });\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"echo-stack\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
